---
import type { CasePart } from "../types";
import graphicalAbstract from "./acta-graphical-abstract.svg";
import { actaFigure as figure } from "./acta-figure-data";

interface Props {
  part: CasePart;
}
const { part } = Astro.props;
---

{part === "intro" && (
  <p>
    My contributions included experimental design, PsychoPy task development,
    behavioral data collection, and analysis in Python and R.
  </p>
)}

{part === "visual" && (
  <figure class="portfolio-figure acta-figure">
    <img
      class="acta-wide"
      src={graphicalAbstract.src}
      width={graphicalAbstract.width}
      height={graphicalAbstract.height}
      alt="Graphical abstract of the reporting task, supervision and incentive experiments, and a published finding. A full text description follows."
      loading="eager"
      decoding="async"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
    <div
      class="acta-narrow portfolio-diagram"
      aria-label="Study design and finding"
    >
      <section>
        <h2>{figure.measureTitle}</h2>
        <ol class="acta-task">
          {figure.task.map((step) => (
            <li>
              <strong>{step.title}</strong>
              <span>{step.detail}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <dl class="acta-comparison">
          <div>
            <dt>{figure.actualLabel}</dt>
            <dd>{figure.actualInput}</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>{figure.reportedLabel}</dt>
            <dd>{figure.reportedInput}</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="acta-relation">{figure.comparison}</p>
        <p class="acta-reward">{figure.reward}</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>{figure.conditionsTitle}</h2>
        <div class="acta-monitoring">
          <h3>Monitoring</h3>
          {figure.monitoring.map((condition) => (
            <p>
              <strong>{condition.title}</strong>
              <span>{condition.detail}</span>
            </p>
          ))}
          <p class="acta-relation">{figure.monitoringContext}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="acta-interventions">
          {figure.interventions.map((condition) => (
            <div class="acta-intervention">
              <h3>{condition.title}</h3>
              <ol>
                {condition.phases.map((phase) => (
                  <li>{phase}</li>
                ))}
              </ol>
            </div>
          ))}
          <p class="acta-relation">{figure.interventionContext}</p>
        </div>
        <p class="acta-traits">{figure.traits}</p>
      </section>
      <section class="acta-finding">
        <h2>{figure.findingsTitle}</h2>
        <p>{figure.finding}</p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      Study design and findings summarized from Wang et al. (2026).
    </figcaption>
    <details class="portfolio-methods acta-description">
      <summary>Figure description</summary>
      <p>{figure.canonicalDescription}</p>
    </details>
  </figure>
)}

{part === "body" && (
  <>
    <h2>Study design</h2>
    <p>
      The task recorded the prediction and outcome, allowing actual correctness
      to be compared with the participant’s report. Claiming a correct
      prediction earned more task tokens.
    </p>
    <p>
      Experiments 1 and 2 examined visible and uncertain monitoring sequentially
      in the same participants. Experiments 3a and 3b examined monetary rewards
      and moral feedback in separate groups. Personality traits were measured
      with the Short Dark Triad (SD3) scale and examined alongside the
      intervention conditions.
    </p>
    <h2>Behavior after reward withdrawal</h2>
    <p>
      In the monetary-reward experiment, extra rewards for consistent honesty
      were introduced and later removed without announcing the rule. The
      comparison separated behavior during reward delivery from persistence
      after withdrawal within the task.
    </p>
    <h2>Published findings</h2>
    <p>
      Honest reporting was higher when monitoring was visible in this task.
      Monetary rewards produced a clearer increase in honest reporting than
      moral feedback, with behavior also varying across measured traits and
      experimental phases.
    </p>
    <details class="portfolio-methods">
      <summary>Trial-level analysis</summary>
      <p>
        One analysis modeled trial-level honesty using supervision conditions,
        personality scores and their interactions, with a participant random
        intercept to account for repeated observations.
      </p>
    </details>
    <h2>Publication</h2>
    <p class="acta-citation">
      Wang, J., Jiang, X., Chen, Y., Wang, M., &amp; Du, F. (2026). From Overt
      Deterrence to Covert Internalization: Moral Effects of AI Regulation and
      the Moderating Role of Personality Traits.{" "}
      <em>Acta Psychologica Sinica, 58</em>(3), 381–398.
    </p>
  </>
)}

<style>
  .acta-figure {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 64rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .acta-wide {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid #c9d5de;
    border-radius: 1rem;
    background: #fcfdfd;
  }
  .acta-narrow {
    display: none;
  }
  .acta-description {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .acta-description p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .acta-citation {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  @media (max-width: 47rem) {
    .acta-wide {
      display: none;
    }
    .acta-narrow {
      display: grid;
      gap: 1.75rem;
      padding: 16px;
      color: var(--portfolio-ink);
      background: var(--portfolio-surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
      border-radius: 1rem;
    }
    .acta-narrow section {
      min-width: 0;
    }
    .acta-narrow h2 {
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      line-height: 1.3;
    }
    .acta-narrow h3 {
      margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
      font-size: 1.0625rem;
      line-height: 1.4;
    }
    .acta-task {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.6rem;
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
    }
    .acta-task li {
      padding-left: 0.25rem;
    }
    .acta-task span,
    .acta-monitoring span {
      display: block;
      color: var(--portfolio-muted);
    }
    .acta-comparison {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.65rem;
      margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    }
    .acta-comparison > div,
    .acta-monitoring,
    .acta-intervention {
      padding: 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
      border-radius: 0.65rem;
    }
    .acta-comparison dt {
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .acta-comparison dd {
      margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
      color: var(--portfolio-muted);
    }
    .acta-relation {
      margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
      color: var(--portfolio-accent);
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .acta-reward {
      margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      color: var(--portfolio-muted);
    }
    .acta-monitoring > p {
      margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
    }
    .acta-interventions {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      margin-top: 0.9rem;
    }
    .acta-intervention ol {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.3rem;
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 1.3rem;
      color: var(--portfolio-muted);
    }
    .acta-traits {
      margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
      padding: 0.8rem 0;
      border-block: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
    }
    .acta-finding p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--portfolio-accent);
    }
  }
</style>
